WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.550
A colleague asked me: where does

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.010
an agent keep its plan, its tool

3
00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.550
calls and its memory?

4
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.020
The answer surprises people.

5
00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.710
It’s all one long text.

6
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.570
Let’s open it up.

7
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.600
Today: inside the loop,

8
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.280
one text at a time.

9
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:22.590
Darsi Tiny reads one text, top to bottom.

10
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.980
Small markers split it into parts: the

11
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.940
tools that are on, your request, its

12
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.500
plan, its call, the result.

13
00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:34.930
Each marker is a single token, and

14
00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.030
nobody can fake one by typing it.

15
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.280
The model writes three kinds of part:

16
00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.500
the plan, the call and the answer.

17
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.160
The app writes everything else: the tools

18
00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.020
line, your request and every result.

19
00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.590
After a call, the model stops and waits.

20
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.880
So the loop is the app,

21
00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:58.620
adding to one text.

22
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.560
It sends the text so far, and

23
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.600
the model writes a call.

24
00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.920
The app runs the tool and adds the result.

25
00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:08.330
Then it sends the text again,

26
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.030
until the model answers.

27
00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:13.910
Ask for the trip from Kafi to

28
00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:16.510
Dala, and the text grows twice.

29
00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.540
First a route call, and its

30
00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:21.680
result: seventy kilometres.

31
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.380
Then a weather call for

32
00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:26.080
Dala, and its result.

33
00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:28.920
Only then does Darsi Tiny

34
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:29.860
write the answer.

35
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:31.700
Quick check!

36
00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:35.930
After Darsi Tiny writes a weather call,

37
00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:38.570
who writes the result into the text?

38
00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.570
The app, from the tool.

39
00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.410
Darsi Tiny was trained to stop

40
00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:46.170
after a call and wait.

41
00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.650
A model that wrote its own result

42
00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.250
would be inventing data, so a

43
00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.890
good app never allows it.

44
00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.770
As code, the loop is only a few lines.

45
00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:01.210
Here the model is scripted: a stand-in

46
00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:03.210
that returns what a model would write.

47
00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:05.840
The code asks for the next part,

48
00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:07.620
and stops at an answer.

49
00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.950
But what if the model never answers?

50
00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:14.460
It could call the same tool again and

51
00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:16.100
again, and the loop would run

52
00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.380
forever, using battery and data.

53
00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.540
So real agents have a step limit,

54
00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.480
then stop and tell the person.

55
00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:27.410
In the app, open What Darsi Tiny

56
00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.850
sees, then press One step.

57
00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.770
Watch the text grow: plan,

58
00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:35.910
call, result, answer.

59
00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:38.650
Then run the trip from Kafi to

60
00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:40.650
Dala, and count the calls.

61
00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:42.470
Your turn.

62
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.700
My agent keeps calling the

63
00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.360
weather tool, and never answers.

64
00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.290
What should the app have?

65
00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.070
A step limit, so the loop

66
00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.690
stops and tells a person.

67
00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:56.340
Remember: it’s all one text, with markers.

68
00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.510
The model writes plans, calls and

69
00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.910
answers, and the app adds the results.

70
00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.490
And every loop needs a stop.

71
00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.880
Try it in class tomorrow: write one agent

72
00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.160
conversation on a long paper strip.

73
00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.930
Model parts in blue, app parts in green.

74
00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.100
Then ask: which colour can make

75
00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.620
mistakes, and where would the app check?
